Bundled FFprobe notice
----------------------

Desktop release bundles include an FFprobe executable so local container
metadata can be read without requiring an operator to install FFmpeg. The
sidecar is obtained at build time from the pinned
[`eugeneware/ffmpeg-static` b6.1.1 release](https://github.com/eugeneware/ffmpeg-static/releases/tag/b6.1.1).
The build script verifies the published SHA-256 for the selected Windows,
Linux, or macOS artifact before it is packaged. The matching upstream FFmpeg
source is [FFmpeg n6.1.1](https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/tree/n6.1.1).

FFprobe is distributed under the GNU General Public License version 3 or
later. This is compatible with this project's AGPL-3.0-or-later distribution.
Each desktop bundle carries the license supplied with its selected FFprobe
artifact. Mobile builds do not package or execute an FFprobe sidecar.
